{"seq": 251, "t_ms": 21822, "type": "verification", "data": {"citations_total": 21, "citations_valid": 21, "numbers_checked": 67, "numbers_traced": 61, "untraced": [{"number": "05:00", "text": "The best-supported maintenance slot in the Bolzano area is early weekday morning, 05:00-07:00 on Thursday, Tuesday or Friday, when pooled occupancy was lowest."}, {"number": "07:00", "text": "The best-supported maintenance slot in the Bolzano area is early weekday morning, 05:00-07:00 on Thursday, Tuesday or Friday, when pooled occupancy was lowest."}, {"number": "4", "text": "These windows rest on only 4-5 comparable dates each, so treat them as a provisional starting point rather than a firm conclusion."}, {"number": "08:00", "text": "- Weekday daytime hours run at roughly 0.4-0.66, for example Thu 08:00 at 0.661, so they are poor slots. [E2]"}, {"number": "07:00", "text": "- BZ_BOEHLER_01 (one point) has a peak local hour of 5 and full_time 0.57, so a 05:00-07:00 slot there needs a site-specific check. [E3]"}, {"number": "07:00", "text": "3. For BZ_BOEHLER_01, choose a different slot or confirm local use before working at 05:00-07:00. [E3]"}], "unknown_ids": []}}
{"seq": 252, "t_ms": 25616, "type": "review_note", "data": {"text": "- **Key caveat:** The 05:00-07:00 slot rests on only 4-5 comparable dates per window (Thu 0.066), pooled across all sites with no per-site profiles. Treat it as a pilot, not a standing schedule.\n- **Overnight blind spot:** 00:00-04:00 is often 0.0 or null (unknown), so quiet is unconfirmed. Coverage is weak (e.g., 0.033-0.147 at top sites).\n- **Untraced values:** The 05:00, 07:00 and 08:00 time labels and the \"4\" in \"4-5 dates\" didn't trace. 61 of 67 numbers traced, and all 21 citations are valid. The untraced items look like formatting, but verify the \"4\" against E2."}}
